A tick box for on/off choices, with a mixed state, groups and a "select all" parent.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/checkbox)

<%= embed AppicaUI::CheckboxPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
label(class: "flex items-center gap-2") do
  Checkbox(name: "terms", checked: true)
  plain "Accept terms and conditions"
end
```

`Checkbox` is a native `<input type="checkbox">`, drawn with Appica's box and animated check: it submits with forms,
toggles with Space and needs no JavaScript. It renders only the box - wrap it and its text in one `<label>`. Native
attributes (`name`, `value`, `required`, `form`, `aria_*`) go to the input; `class:` styles the box. It's sized in
`em`, so it follows the label's text size. `unchecked_value:` adds a hidden fallback so an unticked box still
submits (like Rails' `check_box`).

